From 91bb5bdf9976efa39e294d1295dc146c2770f81c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 08:53:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Screen layouts and stylus mode for nuubOS

- Layouts Large Top/Large Bottom (one screen at twice the size across
  the width, the other one below it at its own size) and Picture in
  Picture Top/Bottom (one screen filling the picture at three times the
  size, the other one at its own size over its bottom right corner, three
  parts opaque to one). R2 swaps them like the others; a toggled swap
  stays across option changes. The geometry's maximum is the largest
  layout, so changing layouts never reinitialises the video.
- Core option melonds_nuubos_stylus (off, right, left, dpad): a cursor
  moved with that control (sticks: dead zone, then quadratic up to
  5 px a frame; D-pad: slow, then faster while held), L2 touches; it
  overrides the touch mode and the D-pad stops reaching the game when it
  moves the cursor. nuubOS switches it live with a hotkey.
- The left stick works as the D-pad in the core (RetroArch stops doing
  it once a core reads an analog stick).
- The cursor is a white cross-hair with a black border, scaled with the
  touch screen (the 4x4 inverted square disappeared on mid greys).
